WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.930 --> 00:00:07.900
Here are the best viral
products I tested in 2021.

00:00:07.900 --> 00:00:09.190
Let's start with brows.

00:00:09.190 --> 00:00:11.680
The Huda Beauty #BombBrows
Microshade Brow Pencil

00:00:11.680 --> 00:00:13.450
has this incredibly thin point

00:00:13.450 --> 00:00:16.140
that makes it so easy to
make hairlike strokes.

00:00:16.140 --> 00:00:17.270
It is a little fragile,

00:00:17.270 --> 00:00:19.370
so be careful with how
much pressure you're using,

00:00:19.370 --> 00:00:21.010
but I love this pencil.

00:00:21.010 --> 00:00:23.630
If you struggle with using
pencils to fill in your brows,

00:00:23.630 --> 00:00:26.630
I highly recommend this
Madluvv Brow Stamp Kit.

00:00:26.630 --> 00:00:28.532
You apply one of the stencils to your brow

00:00:28.532 --> 00:00:30.490
and stamp the brow color on to fill.

00:00:30.490 --> 00:00:33.200
It makes doing your
brows so fast and easy,

00:00:33.200 --> 00:00:34.388
and you don't have to worry about

00:00:34.388 --> 00:00:36.440
having two different brow shapes.

00:00:36.440 --> 00:00:38.520
Now my favorite brow-setting products.

00:00:38.520 --> 00:00:41.090
Everyone went nuts for
the ABH Brow Freeze,

00:00:41.090 --> 00:00:41.923
and so did I.

00:00:41.923 --> 00:00:44.400
It gives your brows that
fluffy, laminated look

00:00:44.400 --> 00:00:46.830
and keeps the hair
locked in place all day.

00:00:46.830 --> 00:00:49.400
But I recently tried the ELF Brow Lift,

00:00:49.400 --> 00:00:52.160
and I swear it works exactly the same.

00:00:52.160 --> 00:00:54.490
It also came out with
this special applicator

00:00:54.490 --> 00:00:57.060
that really lets you
press those hairs down.

00:00:57.060 --> 00:00:58.670
Moving on to complexion products,

00:00:58.670 --> 00:01:01.140
the Fenty Beauty Eaze
Drop Blurring Skin Tint

00:01:01.140 --> 00:01:03.831
is so natural and beautiful on the skin.

00:01:03.831 --> 00:01:06.520
The coverage is minimal
but very buildable.

00:01:06.520 --> 00:01:09.420
The L'Oréal True Match Nude
Hyaluronic Tinted Serum

00:01:09.420 --> 00:01:10.950
is another great option.

00:01:10.950 --> 00:01:12.100
It evens out the skin

00:01:12.100 --> 00:01:14.970
and gives you a very
glowy, hydrated finish.

00:01:14.970 --> 00:01:17.959
Plus you get the added
benefits of hyaluronic acid.

00:01:17.959 --> 00:01:19.576
The Pseudo Labs PHreckles Kit

00:01:19.576 --> 00:01:21.151
is definitely the best product

00:01:21.151 --> 00:01:23.532
I've ever used for creating faux freckles.

00:01:23.532 --> 00:01:24.780
You use the freckle liquid,

00:01:24.780 --> 00:01:26.850
which has this little round brush in it

00:01:26.850 --> 00:01:28.762
and this little toothpick-looking thing

00:01:28.762 --> 00:01:30.480
to flick the liquid onto your face,

00:01:30.480 --> 00:01:33.420
and it gives you these very
natural-looking freckles.

00:01:33.420 --> 00:01:35.712
This Givenchy Prisme Libre Loose Powder

00:01:35.712 --> 00:01:37.336
is a huge splurge item

00:01:37.336 --> 00:01:39.050
that actually lived up to the hype.

00:01:39.050 --> 00:01:41.460
The colors all blend into
one translucent shade

00:01:41.460 --> 00:01:43.242
that really brightens up the under-eyes

00:01:43.242 --> 00:01:45.830
and sets the face without
leaving you feeling dry.

00:01:45.830 --> 00:01:48.152
It makes the skin looks so smooth.

00:01:48.152 --> 00:01:50.683
Next, my favorite makeup product, blush.

00:01:50.683 --> 00:01:52.930
I tried so many different kinds this year.

00:01:52.930 --> 00:01:54.480
I think my favorite was definitely

00:01:54.480 --> 00:01:56.740
the Melt Cosmetics Cream Blushlight.

00:01:56.740 --> 00:02:00.060
This formula is pigmented
and blended like a dream.

00:02:00.060 --> 00:02:03.210
It layered over powder
really, really nicely.

00:02:03.210 --> 00:02:05.042
The Em Cosmetics So Soft blush

00:02:05.042 --> 00:02:07.750
is also a cream blush,
but in a stick form.

00:02:07.750 --> 00:02:09.822
This one is very user-friendly.

00:02:09.822 --> 00:02:12.070
Because it is so soft
and easy to blend out,

00:02:12.070 --> 00:02:14.070
you don't have to worry
about overdoing it.

00:02:14.070 --> 00:02:16.405
The Made by Mitchell Blursh Liquid Blusher

00:02:16.405 --> 00:02:18.438
is probably the best liquid-blush formula

00:02:18.438 --> 00:02:19.787
I've ever tried.

00:02:19.787 --> 00:02:22.460
I applied this over my
already-set foundation,

00:02:22.460 --> 00:02:24.390
and it still blended out so well

00:02:24.390 --> 00:02:26.360
without removing any product underneath,

00:02:26.360 --> 00:02:28.850
and the pigment is so intense.

00:02:28.850 --> 00:02:30.050
Now on to bronzer.

00:02:30.050 --> 00:02:31.000
Just like the blush,

00:02:31.000 --> 00:02:33.200
Em Cosmetics So Soft Multi Faceplay

00:02:33.200 --> 00:02:35.330
is creamy and easy to use.

00:02:35.330 --> 00:02:37.860
The shade I got was more
of a contour color for me,

00:02:37.860 --> 00:02:40.370
but there are some warmer
shades for bronzing.

00:02:40.370 --> 00:02:43.050
The ELF Putty Bronzer is
another amazing bronzer,

00:02:43.050 --> 00:02:44.510
and an affordable one.

00:02:44.510 --> 00:02:47.180
The blendability of
this bronzer is unreal.

00:02:47.180 --> 00:02:49.177
It has this really interesting formula

00:02:49.177 --> 00:02:52.268
that goes from a cream to
more of a powder finish.

00:02:52.268 --> 00:02:54.185
It's so easy to work with.

00:02:54.185 --> 00:02:56.540
Next, we have some really
interesting eye products.

00:02:56.540 --> 00:02:58.710
These Chameleon Flakes
from Kaima Cosmetics

00:02:58.710 --> 00:03:01.420
are like little shavings of
pigment that shift color.

00:03:01.420 --> 00:03:03.500
They definitely have a
bit of a learning curve,

00:03:03.500 --> 00:03:06.110
but once you get it, they
look amazing on the eyes.

00:03:06.110 --> 00:03:08.330
This product is technically
a multiuse product,

00:03:08.330 --> 00:03:09.760
but I'm putting it here.

00:03:09.760 --> 00:03:12.070
This is the Danessa
Myricks Beauty Colorfix

00:03:12.070 --> 00:03:14.060
eye, cheek, and lip cream pigment.

00:03:14.060 --> 00:03:16.870
The pigment in these is no joke.

00:03:16.870 --> 00:03:18.570
A little goes such a long way.

00:03:18.570 --> 00:03:19.870
And the fact that you can use them

00:03:19.870 --> 00:03:22.310
as so many different
things, under-eye corrector,

00:03:22.310 --> 00:03:24.385
blush, eyeliner, lipstick, eye shadow,

00:03:24.385 --> 00:03:26.151
is definitely a plus.

00:03:26.151 --> 00:03:29.370
And finally, a few of the
best lip products I tried.

00:03:29.370 --> 00:03:32.190
If you want that full-coverage,
transfer-proof lip,

00:03:32.190 --> 00:03:35.310
definitely check out
the NYX Lip Lingerie XXL

00:03:35.310 --> 00:03:36.780
matte liquid lipsticks.

00:03:36.780 --> 00:03:38.720
One thin layer is all you need,

00:03:38.720 --> 00:03:40.930
and once they dry down,
they're not moving.

00:03:40.930 --> 00:03:42.840
The Milani Color Fetish matte lipstick

00:03:42.840 --> 00:03:45.680
is also very pigmented
and wears really nicely.

00:03:45.680 --> 00:03:47.430
These aren't as matte as you would think,

00:03:47.430 --> 00:03:49.120
and they still have that comfortable slip

00:03:49.120 --> 00:03:51.023
that you'd get from a regular lipstick.

